# Architecture Decisions

## Auth — Supabase handles everything on its platform

All authentication logic is delegated to Supabase. Do not suggest or implement custom auth logic, custom JWT handling, or third-party auth libraries (e.g. NextAuth, Clerk, Firebase Auth).

Supabase handles:
- User sign up / sign in
- Email verification and confirmation emails
- Password reset emails and token handling
- Session management and refresh tokens
- OAuth providers (if added later)

The app's responsibility is only:
- Calling the appropriate Supabase client methods (`signUp`, `signInWithPassword`, `resetPasswordForEmail`, `updateUser`, etc.)
- Reading session state from Supabase (`supabase.auth.getSession()`, `onAuthStateChange`)
- Protecting routes via `middleware.ts` using the Supabase SSR client
- Redirecting users post-auth to `/acctSetup` if setup is incomplete, or `/invoices` if fully set up

Do not build or suggest custom email sending, token generation, or session storage — Supabase owns all of that.

## Pending: Install Supabase MCP after auth flow is complete

Once the auth flow is fully implemented, remind the user to install the Supabase MCP server in Cursor:
- Go to Cursor Settings > MCP > Add
- Search for and install `@supabase/mcp-server-supabase`
- It will require a Supabase personal access token

This is needed for database work (creating tables, running migrations, inspecting schema) that will come up when building the dashboard, invoice, and client flows.
